    "q-160292": {
      "dom_id": "step-q160292",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find $|z|$ if $z=-k-2m\\text{i},$ where $k$ and $m$ are real numbers.",
      "worked_solution": "For a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=-k-2m\\text{i},$ we have $a=-k$ and $b=-2m.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|-k-2m\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{(-k)^{2}+(-2m)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{k}^{2}+4{m}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-160292-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\sqrt{k+4m}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"33\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.12em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D458 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msqrt></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-160292-b",
